  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound INDVLXYUCBVVKW-CPEKGPMFSA-N and the CD70 antigen, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with the CD70 antigen. Specifically, the compound is predicted to target DNA polymerase eta, which is then targeted by Ebracteolatanolide A and 2-[(4bS,8aS,9S,10S)-1,9,10-trihydroxy-4b,8,8-trimethyl-3,4-dioxo-5,6,7,8a,9,10-hexahydrophenanthren-2-yl]propyl acetate, both of which are known to target the CD70 antigen. The varying scores across the paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, with the highest scores (0.6216) aligning the compound with the CD70 antigen through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests a mechanistic pathway where the compound may modulate DNA polymerase eta, which in turn influences the CD70 antigen, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets reinforces the likelihood of a broader biological role, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
